cts of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le12ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Offering Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Giving advice in English might seem tricky at first. To talk about what is advisable (what you think should be done), we use <span class=\"strong\">had better</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">might want to</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "These phrases come before the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Subject + had better + verb</span>: You'd better take that back!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Subject + ought to + verb</span>: You ought to think before you speak, you know."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Subject + might want to + verb</span>: You might want to hear yourself."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "touchy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "easily upset; emotionally sensitive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You're so touchy today - take it easy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about people's habits."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "perfectly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a perfect way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm being perfectly calm."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reasonable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "logical; sensible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm being perfectly reasonable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "recklessly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dangerously; without care"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are behaving recklessly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to accuse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to formally say someone did something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You recklessly accuse me of being insensitive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cleverly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a smart way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You cleverly got out of that argument."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sewing machine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a machine used for making clothes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's my antique sewing machine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sewing room"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a room used for making clothes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Shouldn't your sewing machine be in your sewing room?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob02aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span> and<span class=\"strong\"> Would</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about regular events in the past, you can use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> or <span class=\"strong\">would</span>. These are alternative forms from  the Simple Past + Adverbs of frequency.<br/><span class=\"italic\">My grandmother used to like sewing. She would sew for ours.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span> is used for actions (study, work, talk, read, etc.) and for states, or permanent events in the past  (be, have, like, think)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is used for actions only. We never use it to talk about past condition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "She <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> give me advice when I was sad.<br/>She <span class=\"strong\">would</span> give me advice when I was sad."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> be reckless when I was a child. <br/><span style=\"text-decoration:line-through;\">I would be reckless when I was a child.</span>"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, talk about what you used to do with your family when you were a child."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give as many details as you can."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about past habits with my partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give details about what I used to do with my family."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask follow-up questions."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": 